This Act may be called the Indian Evidence Act, 1872.
Extent.––It extends to the whole of India [2][ [3]***] and applies to all judicial proceedings in or before any Court, including Courts-martial, [4][other than Courts-martial convened under the Army Act (44 & 45 Vict., c. 58)][5][the Naval Discipline Act [29 & 30 Vict., 109]; or [6]*** the Indian Navy (Discipline) Act, 1934 (34 of 1934),][7][or the Air Force Act (7 Geo. 5, c. 51)] but not to affidavits[8] presented to any Court or officer, nor to proceedings before an arbitrator;
Commencement of Act.––And it shall come into force on the first day of September, 1872.
